                        <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                        <run fontsize='7'>A client gave me an extract of credit card transactions to analyze and create a forecast of future expenses.  Transactions range from May of 2025 up through and including March of 2026.</run>
                        <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                        <run fontsize='7'>The picture looks bleak. </run>
                        <run bold='true' fontsize='7'>Æ </run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff0000' fontsize='7'>Fear not!</run>
                        <run fontsize='7'> After analysis the forecast for the future is</run>
                        <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                        <run fontsize='7'>not as bleak as it may seem.</run>
                        <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff0000' fontsize='7'>Navigate</run>
                        <run fontsize='7'> to dashboards that answer the questions posed at the project</run>
                        <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                        <run fontsize='7'>outset.</run>
                        <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#ff0000' fontsize='7'>Where is the money spent?</run>
                        <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#ff0000' fontsize='7'>When is it going there?</run>
                        <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#ff0000' fontsize='7'>What is the forecast?</run>
                        <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#ff0000' fontsize='7'>All Transactions</run>
